ed-source anchor for (i) verbatim from Iris Beaumont (U007) Slack message in `#albatross-admin` (`shared/slack_export_halberd/albatross-admin/2026-05-07.json`, 2026-05-07): 'Worst pattern I keep flagging on pre-IC briefings is when the team takes the same point and frames it as both a headline finding and an open question. They're meant to be different beasts: findings are what we now believe; open questions are what we still don't know and need confirmatory to resolve. If a so-called finding has a clear unknown sitting underneath it, it's an open question, not a finding - pick one and move on. The three findings and three open questions should not paraphrase each other across the two groups.' This message lives in the admin channel, not the main `#albatross-deal` channel; (j) every word in the .srt subtitle file and every on-screen text element in the .mp4 (chart labels, lower-thirds, title cards) uses US English spelling; the audio narration is out of scope; proper nouns and registered organisation names retain canonical spelling and do not count as fails.

